<title>ITALY: Agip Petroli has 1996 loss of 253 bln lire - sources.</title>
<headline>Agip Petroli has 1996 loss of 253 bln lire - sources.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agip Petroli Spa, the gasoline distribution arm of Italy's Agip SpA, recorded a net loss of 253 billion lire in 1996 after a 1995 net profit of 114 billion, sources close to the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said the loss was due to expected write-offs. Operating profit in 1996 was 551 billion lire, the sources said.</p>
<p>Agip Petroli's 1996 consolidated group profit was 1.003 trillion lire, up from 870 billion in 1995, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
